  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 155 PM CDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nThe upper low over the Desert Southwest will lift northeast into\nthe central Plains Sunday into Monday. Several disturbances will\nmove the through the area from Sunday through early next week, \nwhich will bring low rain chances to mainly the western half of\nthe forecast area late Sunday into Monday. Additional showers and\na few thunderstorms (20%-40%) will be possible over much of the \narea Monday night into Tuesday as a stronger disturbance in \nsouthwest flow aloft moves through. In addition, temperatures \nwill be cooler Sunday into early next week as cloud cover \nincreases, with highs mainly in the 70s, and lows in the 50s. \n\nWednesday of next week looks dry, then rain chances will increase\nonce again by late week, as we remain in southwest flow aloft \nwith troughing over the western CONUS and several disturbances \nmove through. Temperatures will remain near seasonal values, with \nhighs mainly in the 70s and lows in the 50s.",
